11413	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"review-d24eea8e171fcc4c46b3812644d1cbef","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:17:08.688Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The cutover design covers every backend git/gh caller required by s7.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md explicitly includes 'the understanding identity lookup'. src/understanding/identity.ts still runs gh auth status, gh api users/<login>, and git config --get user.email through an injected runShell. The LLD omits this module from its migration groups, replacement operations and integration subjects. Its GitHub lookup also requires hostname-aware account enumeration and node_id, beyond the proposed current-login operation. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/understanding/identity.ts, .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json]","action":"Add identity lookup to the concrete inventory, replacement contracts, migration tasks and registry-path tests, preserving multi-host/account identity semantics.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"runGitAsync currently preserves a 120-second total refresh deadline.","evidence":"src/workflow/team/sighting-store.ts declares 'REFRESH_DEADLINE_MS = 10_000'. createDeadline in git-async.ts defaults to that constant, and runGitAsync passes remainingMs() as the subprocess timeout. The LLD repeatedly calls 120 seconds the existing budget. Increasing it changes behavior and undermines the lock-lifetime reasoning documented beside REFRESH_DEADLINE_MS. [files: src/workflow/team/git-async.ts, src/workflow/team/sighting-store.ts]","action":"Preserve the 10-second total deadline and its lock assumptions, or explicitly design and authorize the coordinated deadline/locking change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The current artifact commit helper uses the stated order and best-effort push result.","evidence":"The complete commitAndPushArtifacts body checks rev-parse, filters existing paths, adds, tests diff --cached --quiet, commits and pushes in that order. Push failure returns committed:true, pushed:false with 'committed locally; push failed: ...'; the other listed reason prefixes are present. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Retain these checked behaviors in the proposed regression tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The typed call helper and runtime-checked gh family abstraction exist with the stated core shapes.","evidence":"call-tool.ts declares callTool<T extends TypedTool> with Static input/output schemas and the success/failure value union. gh/op-table.ts declares 'GhFamilyTool = TypedTool & { readonly ops: readonly OpDef[] }' and exports defineGhFamily. These are valid reuse points. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Use these existing contracts; specify concrete inputs and outputs for the new tracker operations before implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Common workflow and daemon calls never ask for approval.","evidence":"approval-policy.ts computes 'effective = deps.approvalMode ?? flag' and asks for common calls in manual or edit-auto, without a caller exemption. docs/plans/tool-registry.md supersedes the earlier proposal: callers without a chat session use the global flag. The LLD's §4 claim that these calls 'do not ask' contradicts both. [files: src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Describe common calls as following the effective global/session mode, default auto; preserve denial handling when that mode requires approval.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed inventory comparison remains valid after all listed direct spawns are removed.","evidence":"S007 ac6 requires keeping the list of moved sites. LLD §3.2 instead says the check fails when a listed site is 'no longer present in the old form', while §7 requires deleting those old forms and regenerating the inventory. Successful migration therefore triggers the stated failure condition, or regeneration loses the historical sites needed for coverage. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json]","action":"Separate the retained migration inventory from the current forbidden-spawn scan. Validate replacement/tool/test references and fail on remaining forbidden spawns, not on successful removal of old code.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The new IPC and worker relationships have sufficiently specified contracts for implementation.","evidence":"Existing ToolDeps requires sessionId, repoPath, send and requestId, with daemon-owned connectionExecution. The worker channel already supports correlated requests, replies, cancellation and completion. The LLD names sender and receiver but supplies no exact request/reply union, dependency construction, cancellation/disconnect lifetime, or worker timeout value; it also omits the optional approvalMode required by the recorded s3/s7 decision. The worker transport remains conditional despite being needed by the chosen alternative. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/threads/worker-requests.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Specify exact IPC/channel payloads and ownership of correlation, execution authority, approval mode, cancellation and pending-request cleanup. Prose or a contract table is sufficient; resolve the conditional worker path.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The corpus reader migration preserves its existing binary acquisition and limit contract.","evidence":"readPinnedSources uses lossless Uint8Array responses, recomputes object identities, enforces cumulative metadata/blob budgets and permits lowering a per-process timeout below 30 seconds. createGitRunner isolates the environment and kills the process group. git_cat_file already supports base64, isolation and byte limits, but fixes timeoutMs at 30_000 and maps cancellation to rejected. The LLD explicitly leaves this reader's mapping unsettled, so its promised behavior-preserving cutover is not designed. [files: src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts]","action":"Design the reader-to-tool mapping, including byte decoding, object identity verification, lowered deadlines, error-code translation and process cleanup; preserve existing ReaderOptions and validation results.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"s7 can complete using its declared dependencies without unresolved ownership changes.","evidence":"The DEF lists s7 dependencies as s1 through s5. git/coverage.ts explicitly assigns config, ls-remote, update-ref and rm to s8. The LLD requires those tools but leaves adding s8 or transferring ownership as an open question, and similarly leaves tracker-family ownership unresolved. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/coverage.ts]","action":"Record the dependency/ownership decision in the upstream artifacts before approving this LLD; keep s8 commands with their owner unless scope is explicitly amended.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Passing a deadline signal in ToolDeps bounds running git calls and prevents later calls after expiry.","evidence":"git_fetch_refs.execute accepts only input and calls runShell with 'timeoutMs: 120_000', without deps.signal. git_fetch has the same pattern. executeTool has no general pre-execution aborted-signal check. Merely passing a signal therefore neither kills these running calls nor prevents an already-aborted call from starting, contrary to the proposed refresh error path. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch-refs.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/workflow/team/git-async.ts]","action":"Include signal propagation and pre-abort checks at every relevant execution/precondition path, preserve the actual total deadline, and define cancellation-to-failure mapping.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Destructive denial and post-success hook failures are supported by the executor as described.","evidence":"executeTool returns kind denied before tool.execute for declined, expired, missing-client or cancelled approval. It validates successful data before withHooks; hook failures append report lines and hookFailures while retaining the successful result. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Keep the proposed stage-level tests proving that denial stops subsequent work and hook failure preserves the completed effect.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream acceptance criterion has a proposed proving test.","evidence":"Compared with S007's six acceptance criteria in the DEF, §6 supplies corresponding tests for registry execution, removal/build enforcement, preserved effects, workflow hooks, denied-stage termination and retained inventory. The mapping is present, but its universal per-site promise needs the omitted identity and corpus-reader cases, and the inventory oracle must be corrected as reported above. These are proposed tests, not executed verification. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, src/understanding/identity.ts, src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts, src/workflow/team/git-async.ts]","action":"Retain the six mappings and add explicit deadline/pre-abort, worker failure/cancellation, identity lookup and corpus-reader compatibility cases when repairing those design gaps.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":6,"med":2,"low":4,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T11:17:08.688Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
433	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"50a13558db3949df97658d3534cf3384","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:19:40.887Z","operation":"review","revision":{"number":1,"contentHash":"bf9cff5e4b9354989a8a847c11ba7b77fa1c2686a8995c5733e07c7d4640e1f4"},"outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"reviewed by the daemon: block","data":{"counts":{"high":6,"med":2,"low":4}}}}}
12043	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"review-3a701789045a6a3560c81f1f2f00796c","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:42:53.048Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The replacement tool inventory covers the operations needed to delete all github.ts process wrappers while preserving tracker behavior.","evidence":"github.ts implements queryTasks using GraphQL search with issueCount, hasNextPage and endCursor, and ghCreateOrgIssueType using POST /orgs/{org}/issue-types; setup.ts calls the latter. Neither operation appears in the proposed tracker family. Existing gh_search issues returns a bounded items result rather than the cursor-page contract. Deleting these wrappers without designing replacements loses existing behavior. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/setup.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/account.ts]","action":"Add fixed-schema operations and caller migrations for cursor-based task queries and organization issue-type creation; complete a function-by-function replacement table before deleting github.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Fetch tools currently ignore caller cancellation, and executeTool lacks an already-aborted signal guard.","evidence":"Both fetch implementations call runShell with timeoutMs: 120_000 and no signal. executeTool proceeds from input validation to approval and execution without checking deps.signal.aborted. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch-refs.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Implement the proposed guards and signal propagation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Common approval depends on the effective mode, while destructive approval always asks regardless of caller.","evidence":"shouldAsk returns true for destructive; for common it uses deps.approvalMode ?? flag and asks for manual or edit-auto. executeTool invokes this policy without a caller exemption. [files: src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Preserve this policy during migration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Existing git definitions can be passed unchanged to the stated callTool<T extends TypedTool> helper.","evidence":"TypedTool requires inputSchema: TSchema and a required outputSchema: TSchema, but gitFetchTool, gitCatFileTool and gitRevParseTool are explicitly exported as Tool. Tool exposes inputSchema as Record<string, unknown> and outputSchema as optional. These exports do not satisfy the helper's parameter type, despite having schemas at runtime. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts]","action":"Include definition typing changes that retain concrete schemas, or explicitly design an approved runtime-typed calling contract. Do not solve this with unchecked casts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"gh_auth status supplies the account shape and dependencies assumed by the identity migration.","evidence":"The existing schema is hosts: Array<{host, login, active, state: 'logged-in' | 'failed'}>, whereas the design repeatedly specifies checking state success. buildAuthStatus uses ghConvert with required: true; ghConvert fails with 'no conversion provider is configured' when deps.conversion is absent. The proposed ToolDeps construction does not supply conversion providers. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/account.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/convert.ts, src/understanding/identity.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Specify adaptation from the actual flat host/account schema, including logged-in state, and wire daemon-owned conversion providers for identity and auth calls.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The inventory and scan enforce that every workflow tool invocation passes through the executor.","evidence":"grounding.ts calls 'await gitDiffTool.execute({ cwd: repoPath, ...input }, toolDeps)' and changed-files.ts does the same. Neither appears in the migration record or integration subjects. docs/plans/tool-registry.md explicitly names both as s7 migrations. A scan for spawns and old wrappers will not detect these direct execute bypasses. [files: src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Add both sites and their callers/tests to the inventory, and detect direct builtin execute calls outside the executor where they bypass approval, hooks and validation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Changing the two fetch tools is sufficient to preserve the refresh's total deadline and cancellation contract.","evidence":"refreshLocked also resolves revisions, reads a tree and policy content, finds an anchor and updates symbolic refs. git_rev_parse calls readGit with a fixed 10_000 ms and no deps; git_symbolic_ref calls runShell with a fixed 10_000 ms and no signal; git_show performs calls with 15_000/30_000 ms limits and no signal. The design promises cancellation for every refresh call but specifies concrete changes only for fetch and cat-file. [files: src/workflow/team/policy-refresh.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/symbolic-ref.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/show.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts]","action":"Inventory every refresh and anchor operation, name its replacement tool, and explicitly add signal/deadline propagation to all subprocesses it can start, including multi-command tools.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed corpus failure translation preserves existing SourceReaderError codes and messages.","evidence":"createGitRunner currently reports stdout overflow as limit.exceeded/'Git output exceeds byte limit.' and stderr overflow as limit.exceeded/'Git diagnostics exceed byte limit.'. git_cat_file reports these conditions as rejected, while the design maps rejected and remaining failures to inventory.invalid or reference.missing. Thus the stated translation changes observable validation results for valid lower reader budgets. [files: src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts]","action":"Define explicit translations for output, diagnostic and object-size limit failures, missing objects, malformed frames and cancellation; preserve the current codes/messages and add regression cases using lowered ReaderOptions limits.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The two exemptions and s7 ownership of the tracker family and four git commands are authorized upstream scope refinements.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md records the 2026-10-26 decisions: indexer exemption beside self-update, s7 tracker family, and s7 config/ls-remote/update-ref/rm without adding s8 as a dependency. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Keep these decisions linked from the implementation and coverage records.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Hardcoding tools.call caller to workflow preserves the shared IPC contract.","evidence":"The s3 built-contract section states the request 'MUST carry caller' with agent, daemon or workflow and that the daemon must set deps.caller from it. The proposed request omits caller and always sets workflow, despite declaring sc4 unchanged. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Preserve the documented caller field and validate its enum, or record an explicit shared-contract amendment separating the terminal-only method from the general tool-call surface.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.3","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design adequately documents the new IPC interaction and ownership without requiring a separate ERD.","evidence":"Against the existing server's connection controller, inflight cancellation and request lifetime model, §3.5 identifies terminal-to-daemon direction, one request/result exchange, daemon-owned dependencies, connection-owned cancellation and approval routing. No persistent entity relationship is introduced. No visual companion is linked for rendering verification. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"A sequence diagram is optional; retain this ownership detail while resolving the contract findings.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"A single aborted-signal check before approval guarantees that no tool starts after cancellation or the deadline.","evidence":"executeTool awaits buildApprovalRequest and gate().ask before invoking tool.execute. Cancellation can occur during those awaits or immediately after an approval is returned. The proposed pre-approval check does not cover this interval, and several reused tools do not inspect the signal themselves. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts]","action":"Recheck cancellation immediately before tool.execute, propagate it through every relevant subprocess helper, and test cancellation during preview construction and approval completion.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream s7 acceptance criterion has an explicit proving-test category in the design.","evidence":"DEF §6.7 defines ac1–ac6 for executor migration, removal/build enforcement, behavioral parity, hooks, denial and retained inventory. The design's acceptance mapping addresses all six with per-site execution, scanner controls, effect comparison, hook invocation, denial stopping and inventory checks. Existing fake-gh infrastructure supports the proposed binary fixture approach. This verifies mapping completeness, not implemented test coverage. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/_fakegh.ts]","action":"Extend the mapped cases to cover the missing operations, bypass sites and compatibility failures identified above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":7,"med":1,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T11:42:53.048Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
